# Debugging with local-backend logs

## How it fits together
- `npm run dev` (repo root) starts **local-backend** (Fastify, http://localhost:8787) and **Vite** (http://localhost:5173). Vite proxies `/api/*` and `/ws` to the backend, so the browser never calls Google directly.
- The backend mocks Google Cloud locally:
  - Firestore → SQLite at `local-backend/data/firestore.sqlite3` (table `docs`: collection, id, data JSON, updated)
  - Cloud Storage → files under `local-backend/data/storage/uploads/<uid>/<id>/`
  - Auth → stub user `local-user` (override with the `X-User-Id` header)
  - Jobs → in-process, status in `jobs/{id}` docs
- Gemini is **real**: Vertex AI, project `krayon-ai`, location `global`, model `gemini-2.5-flash` (review model `gemini-2.5-pro`), using gcloud Application Default Credentials (`GEMINI_API_KEY` is only a fallback). Config lives in `local-backend/.env`.
- Course generation: upload via `POST /api/courses`, then Genkit flows in `local-backend/src/flows/` (roadmap, lesson, segmentLoop). Live events arrive on `/ws`. `npm run genkit` opens the Genkit trace UI.
- Fallback when `VITE_USE_BACKEND=false`: `frontend/src/lib/ai.ts` still uploads once and calls `POST /api/ai/generate`.
- Reset everything: `curl -X POST localhost:8787/api/admin/reset` (local dev only; also the header's "Clear resources" button, which clears `krayon.*` localStorage too).
- Tests: `npm run test:backend` (full, real Vertex calls) or `npm run test:backend:quick` (no AI). Script: `local-backend/test/smoke.test.ts`.

## Logs
Location: `local-backend/logs/` (gitignored; rotate at 5 MB × 5). The same lines also go to the console (the `[backend]` prefix in `npm run dev`).
- `app.log`: human-readable: `2026-10-17 01:10:59,182 ERROR [<request_id>] <logger>: <message> {json extras}`, tracebacks inline.
- `app.jsonl`: one JSON object per line. Common keys: `ts`, `level`, `logger`, `request_id`, `msg`, `event`, `exc` (traceback).

Events (`event` key):
- `response` (logger `krayon.http`), one per request: `method`, `path`, `query`, `user`, `status`, `duration_ms`, `request_headers` (auth/cookie redacted), `request_body`, `response_body`. Bodies are truncated to `LOG_BODY_MAX`; uploads log `{filename, content_type, size}`, never bytes. Level: INFO for 2xx/3xx, WARNING for 4xx, ERROR for 5xx.
- `error`: an unhandled exception, with `exc`. The client gets 500 `{"detail", "requestId"}`.
- `gemini` (`krayon.gemini`): `backend`, `model`, `prompt_chars`, `file_bytes`, `file_type`, `has_schema`, `latency_ms`, `usage{prompt,output,thoughts,total}`, `finish_reason`, or `error` plus `exc` on failure.
- `job`: `job_id`, `kind`, `status` (queued, running, done, error), `duration_ms`.
- Pipeline steps also carry `courseId`, `topicId`, `segmentId`, `round`, `flow`, and `step`.
- `reset`: counts wiped by `/api/admin/reset`.
- `startup`: AI backend, project, location, data dir.
- At DEBUG only: `docstore.get|set|delete|list|clear`, `storage.put|get|clear`, `gemini.text` (raw model output).

Every response carries an `X-Request-ID` header. Send your own `X-Request-ID` to choose the id; the id also propagates into job logs.

## Recipes
```bash
cd local-backend/logs
tail -f app.log                                              # live
grep '<request_id>' app.log                                  # everything for one request
jq -c 'select(.request_id=="<id>")' app.jsonl                # same, structured
jq -c 'select(.level=="ERROR" or .level=="WARNING") | {ts,request_id,msg,status,error}' app.jsonl
jq -r 'select(.exc) | .ts + " " + .request_id + "\n" + .exc' app.jsonl          # tracebacks
jq -c 'select(.event=="gemini") | {ts,model,latency_ms,usage,file_type,error}' app.jsonl
jq -c 'select(.event=="response" and .path=="/api/ai/generate") | {request_id,status,duration_ms}' app.jsonl
jq -c 'select(.event=="response") | select(.duration_ms > 5000) | {path,duration_ms}' app.jsonl
curl -si localhost:8787/api/health | grep -i x-request-id    # get an id, then grep it
```
In the browser: the Network tab shows `X-Request-ID` on every `/api` response. Grep for it.

## Settings (`local-backend/.env`)
- `LOG_LEVEL`: `INFO` by default; `DEBUG` adds docstore, storage and raw Gemini output.
- `LOG_BODY_MAX`: maximum characters of each body (default 2000).
- `LOG_DIR`: default `./logs`.
- `GEMINI_REVIEW_MODEL`, `MAX_REPAIR_ROUNDS`, `MAX_REVIEW_ROUNDS`, `REVIEW_PASS_SCORE`, `TOPIC_CONCURRENCY`, `RENDER_KEYFRAMES_MAX` control the segment loop.
Restart the backend after changing them.

## Rules for agents
- Check `app.jsonl` for the failing request id before guessing; quote the relevant lines.
- Never print or log secrets. The logger masks keys matching authorization, cookie, api key, token, secret, password or credential, plus `AIza…`, `ya29.…` and `Bearer …` values. Don't add a field whose key contains "token" if you want it visible (that's why Gemini usage is logged under `usage`).
- Don't reset data (`/api/admin/reset`) or delete `data/` unless the user asks.
